From: yuzu <yuzu23234@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] apps_mem: preserve 64-bit DSP heap addresses

The stock SM8150 ARM64 library returns the complete remote_mmap64 result
through apps_mem_request_map64. Preserve its upper bits in the 64-bit
output instead of truncating the address to 32 bits.

--- a/hexagonrpcd/apps_mem.c
+++ b/hexagonrpcd/apps_mem.c
@@ -90,7 +90,7 @@
 #endif
 
 	first_out->vapps = 0;
-	first_out->vadsp = mmap.vaddrout & 0xFFFFFFFF;
+	first_out->vadsp = mmap.vaddrout;
 	return 0;
 }
 
